{
  "about": [
    "Hand-written travel facts for tools/lib/travel.js. Noir Guides, GPLv3. See LICENSE.",
    "links: boats, zeppelins, the tram and the Skyborne skycutters. Each end is a zone (AreaTable ID) and map percent.",
    "  verified = true only when nothing about the link is assumed: the client's own transport path (TaxiPathNode rows",
    "  of the TaxiPath in 'path') stops at both ends, which tools/test/travel.test.js checks, and who may board and how",
    "  is a public fact of the original game. Times are estimates for every link and are not part of 'verified'.",
    "  A link with verified = false names what is not confirmed in 'assumed'; the loader refuses a link that is verified",
    "  and assumes something, and one that is neither. 'assumed' can name:",
    "    route     that it runs between these two ends (no client path, or the client paths disagree)",
    "    factions  who may board (Forever's own routes: no public fact says)",
    "    boarding  the conditions in 'requires' and 'oneWay'",
    "    arrival   the exact place it arrives at",
    "    kind      what it is (a ship, or the portal object at the same dock)",
    "  travelPlan copies verified and assumed onto every transport leg, and plans without unverified links when asked.",
    "  A link without 'path' carries its own 'seconds' (wait and ride together), which is an estimate.",
    "passes: where one zone can be left for the next on foot. All of them are approximate and verified = false;",
    "  source 'map' is the public world map, source 'spawns' is the place where both zones' creature lists meet.",
    "docs/routes/TRAVEL-NOTES.md lists the evidence and everything the owner has to confirm in game."
  ],
