      "note": "Quest 95349 calls it the skycutter ship; object 716302 'Portal to Thunder Bluff' stands at the same dock. The same is confirmed and assumed as for the Alliance skycutter: planned as a ship, one way and only with the quest." },
    { "id": "portal-dalaran-stormwind", "kind": "portal", "name": "Skyborne Portal to Stormwind",
      "a": { "zone": 36, "x": 12.0, "y": 56.2 }, "b": { "zone": 1519, "x": 70.5, "y": 73.5 },
      "factions": ["Alliance"], "verified": false, "assumed": ["route", "boarding", "arrival"], "seconds": 40, "oneWay": true,
      "requires": { "quest": 94947 },
      "note": "Quest 94947 'Welcome to Azeroth' says: take the Skyborne Portal to Stormwind and report to Bolvar Fordragon. Its objective is object 631299 'Skyborne Portal to Stormwind', which the data places in Alterac Mountains 12.04, 56.21, beside the quest's giver. The quest is the High Order's, so the faction stands. Not confirmed: that the portal leads to Stormwind ('route': a portal has no client path), that it needs the quest and does not lead back ('boarding'), and where in Stormwind it ends ('arrival'): the end given here is the last node of client path 11350, which runs from Dalaran to Stormwind without stops. The 40 seconds are a walk through and a loading screen." }
